            <h2 id="section2">🔍 China's Rhinoplasty Landscape</h2>

            <h3>Rhinoplasty Techniques Available in China</h3>

            <h4>1. Closed Rhinoplasty (Endonasal)</h4>
            <p>The most common technique in China. All incisions are made inside the nostrils, leaving no visible scarring. Ideal for patients requiring dorsal augmentation, tip refinement, or minor septum corrections. Recovery time is typically 7-14 days.</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Advantages:</strong> No external scars, faster recovery, less swelling</li>
                <li><strong>Best for:</strong> Asian rhinoplasty (augmentation), mild to moderate corrections</li>
                <li><strong>Recovery:</strong> 7-14 days initial, 3-6 months final</li>
            </ul>

            <h4>2. Open Rhinoplasty (External)</h4>
            <p>A small incision is made across the columella (the skin between the nostrils), providing direct visualization of nasal structures. Allows for more complex reshaping and is preferred for revision cases or significant structural changes.</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Advantages:</strong> Better visualization, more precise shaping, suitable for complex cases</li>
                <li><strong>Best for:</strong> Revision rhinoplasty, significant tip refinement, complex structural work</li>
                <li><strong>Recovery:</strong> 10-21 days initial, 6-12 months final</li>
            </ul>

            <h4>3. Dorsal Augmentation (Asian Rhinoplasty)</h4>
            <p>Specifically designed for patients with flatter nasal bridges (common in East Asian populations). Uses silicone implants, Goretex, or autologous cartilage (rib, ear, or septum) to increase nasal bridge height and definition.</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Implants:</strong> Silicone (L-shaped or I-shaped), Goretex/ePTFE, Medpor</li>
                <li><strong>Autologous options:</strong> Septal cartilage, ear cartilage, rib cartilage</li>
                <li><strong>Cost range:</strong> ¥18,000-45,000 ($2,500-6,200)</li>
