            <h2 id="section8">⚠️ Risks, Contraindications & Who Should NOT Have Rhinoplasty</h2>

            <p>Like any surgical procedure, rhinoplasty carries risks. Understanding these and knowing your contraindications is essential for making an informed decision.</p>

            <h3>Clinical Risks & Complication Rates</h3>

            <div class="risk-grid">
                <div class="risk-item">
                    <h5>Infection</h5>
                    <p><strong>Rate:</strong> &lt;1% (with proper antibiotic prophylaxis)</p>
                    <p>Usually responds to antibiotics. Rare cases may require implant removal.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="risk-item">
                    <h5>Revision Rate</h5>
                    <p><strong>Rate:</strong> 5-15% (primary), 15-30% (revision cases)</p>
                    <p>May be needed for aesthetic refinement or functional correction.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="risk-item">
                    <h5>Septal Perforation</h5>
                    <p><strong>Rate:</strong> 1-3%</p>
                    <p>Hole in the nasal septum causing whistling sound, crusting, or bleeding.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="risk-item">
                    <h5>Implant Extrusion/Migration</h5>
                    <p><strong>Rate:</strong> 2-5% (silicone), &lt;1% (autologous)</p>
                    <p>Implant may shift position or break through skin over time.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="risk-item">
                    <h5>Numbness/Sensory Changes</h5>
                    <p><strong>Rate:</strong> 5-10% temporary, &lt;1% permanent</p>
                    <p>Usually resolves within 3-6 months.</p>
                </div>
                <div class="risk-item">
                    <h5>Breathing Difficulties</h5>
                    <p><strong>Rate:</strong> 3-8%</p>
                    <p>May require septoplasty or turbinate reduction to correct.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <h3>Absolute Contraindications (Do NOT Have Surgery)</h3>
            <div class="highlight-box danger">
                <p><strong>🚫 You should NOT have rhinoplasty if you:</strong></p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Have uncontrolled hypertension or cardiovascular disease</li>
                    <li>Have a bleeding disorder (hemophilia, von Willebrand disease) or are on blood thinners that cannot be stopped</li>
                    <li>Have an active nasal infection or sinus infection</li>
                    <li>Have autoimmune diseases affecting wound healing (lupus, scleroderma)</li>
                    <li>Are pregnant or breastfeeding</li>
                    <li>Have unrealistic expectations about outcomes</li>
                    <li>Are under 18 years old (skeletal maturity not reached)</li>
                    <li>Have severe untreated mental health conditions affecting judgment</li>
                    <li>Have cocaine or methamphetamine use (causes nasal damage)</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <h3>Relative Contraindications (Proceed With Caution)</h3>
            <div class="highlight-box warning">
                <p><strong>⚠️ Conditions requiring careful evaluation:</strong></p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Diabetes (must be well-controlled)</li>
                    <li>Smoking (must quit 2-4 weeks before and after surgery)</li>
                    <li>Previous rhinoplasty with significant scar tissue</li>
                    <li>Thin skin that may show implant edges</li>
                    <li>Severe septal deviation</li>
                    <li>Allergies to implant materials (consider autologous options)</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <h3>Minimizing Your Risks</h3>
            <div class="highlight-box success">
                <p><strong>✅ To minimize risks:</strong></p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Choose a board-certified surgeon at a JCI-accredited hospital</li>
                    <li>Disclose complete medical history including medications and supplements</li>
                    <li>Follow pre-operative and post-operative instructions precisely</li>
                    <li>Stop smoking at least 2 weeks before surgery</li>
                    <li>Avoid blood-thinning medications (aspirin, ibuprofen) 2 weeks before</li>
                    <li>Ensure adequate recovery time before strenuous activity</li>
                    <li>Attend all follow-up appointments, even if feeling fine</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

